Humdinger Piano Samples Provenance & Notice
==========================================

The audio files in this directory (`mf_022.wav` through `mf_106.wav`) were
generated by `scripts/prepare_piano.exs` from the University of Iowa
Electronic Music Studios Musical Instrument Samples (MIS) piano recordings
(Steinway Model B, mezzo-forte `mf` dynamic series, B0 through Bb7; `mf_022.wav`
for Bb0 derived by pitching down B0 one semitone).

Upstream source archive:
  https://theremin.music.uiowa.edu/sound%20files/MIS/Piano_Other/piano/

Processing applied in `scripts/prepare_piano.exs`:
- Downmixed to mono, resampled to 22050 Hz 16-bit PCM WAV.
- Onset-trimmed (44-sample pre-attack lead-in), duration-tapered (3.2 s at
  MIDI 22 to 1.0 s at MIDI 106 with a 250 ms raised-cosine tail), and
  loudness-normalized across roots.

Attribution & Publisher Permission:
  Created by Lawrence Fritts, Director of the Electronic Music Studios and
  Professor of Composition at the University of Iowa.

  Authoritative publisher page (permission statement verified by supervisor on
  2026-11-15):
    https://theremin.music.uiowa.edu/MIS.html

  Verbatim publisher statement:
    "The University of Iowa Musical Instrument Samples (MIS) are created by
    Lawrence Fritts, Director of the Electronic Music Studios and Professor of
    Composition at the University of Iowa. Since 1997, these recordings have
    been freely available on this website and may be downloaded and used for
    any projects, without restrictions. These are used by musicians,
    application developers, teachers, students, and researchers."
